      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Rye never incorporated; it functions as a statistical entity rather than a formal municipal government.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/rye_arkansas",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Loamy, alluvial soils in Rye support soybeans and pine timber, making agriculture and forestry key industries.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/rye_arkansas",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Rye’s humid subtropical climate brings about 55 inches of rain annually and a 215‑day growing season from late March to early November.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/rye_arkansas",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Spring thunderstorms raise tornado risk, and the Saline River can flood low‑lying areas in Rye.",
